.Dd November 15, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-UNBOX 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-unbox
.Nd open a file sealed with noqtis box
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis unbox
.Fl k Ar key
.Fl o Ar out
.Op Fl c Ar ctx
.Op Fl s Ar sender.pub | Fl -any-sender
.Op Fl -pass-fd Ar n | Fl -pass-env Ar name
.Op Fl f | Fl -force
.Ar file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm noqtis unbox
decrypts what
.Xr noqtis-box 1
wrote,
.Ar file
or standard input for
.Ar - ,
with the ML-KEM secret key in
.Ar key ,
to
.Ar out
(created owner-only, mode 0600) or standard output for
.Ar - .
Each chunk is written only after its tag has verified.
When a chunk does not verify (the file was changed, cut, reordered or
lengthened, or is not for this key or context), the command stops with
exit status 2 and removes
.Ar out ,
as it does when stopped by a signal
.Xr noqtis 1
lists as handled under SIGNALS:
the plaintext is written under a temporary name beside
.Ar out
and renamed only once whole
.Pq Xr noqtis 1 ;
on standard output, what was written had verified but the data is cut
short, so check the exit status before using it.
A header that names a chunk size outside 1024 to 16777216 bytes is
refused before anything is allocated.
.Pp
A file sealed to several keys opens with the secret key of any one of
them.
A file its sender signed
.Pq Xr noqtis-box 1 Fl s
is opened only with
.Fl s ,
the sender's public key, or with
.Fl -any-sender ;
the signature is the last thing in the file, so the plaintext is
written before it is checked, and
.Ar out
exists only once it verified.
On standard output the plaintext is the sender's only when the exit
status is 0.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl k Ar key , Fl -key Ns = Ns Ar key
The ML-KEM secret key file.
.It Fl o Ar out , Fl -out Ns = Ns Ar out
The output file, or
.Ar - .
.It Fl c Ar ctx , Fl -ctx Ns = Ns Ar ctx
The context string given to
.Xr noqtis-box 1 .
.It Fl s Ar sender.pub , Fl -sender Ns = Ns Ar sender.pub
The sender's public signature key: the file must be signed, and the
signature must verify under this key.
A file that is not signed is refused.
.It Fl -any-sender
Open a signed file without checking who signed it.
.It Fl -pass-fd Ar n , Fl -pass-env Ar name
The passphrase of a protected key, as in
.Xr noqtis-dec 1 .
.It Fl f , Fl -force
Replace an existing output file.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when every chunk verified, and with
.Fl s
the sender's signature too; 2 otherwise, or on a usage, key or file
error.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-box 1 ,
.Xr nqkfeini 3 ,
.Xr nqkmeini 3
